# User welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
# Date 1786995300 -3600
# Node ID 8cb8001c3dfe02f4396eab24040528954c34965a
# Parent  8aa33d0b94ad89e7c2eea2a2d8c914e861aefa64
Bug 450059 - Don't call endFolderLoading on folders being deleted. r=mkmelin

When the folder displayed by a DBViewWrapper is deleted, the wrapper is
notified via FolderNotificationHelper and calls close(true). The
folderIsDead flag already existed to avoid calling back into the dying
folder (onLeavingFolder is skipped for dead folders), but the folder
loading state was still torn down unconditionally, which called
endFolderLoading() on the deleted folder.

endFolderLoading() re-registers the folder as a DB change listener and
runs UpdateSummaryTotals(true), which calls FlushToFolderCache(). For a
folder that is being deleted this is harmful: RecursiveDelete has just
removed the folder's entry from the folder cache and its summary file,
and the stale folder object (still alive via strong references) would
re-write its entry - including the Virtual flag, which is still set on
the dying object. When a new folder is later created with the same name,
it then incorrectly reads the Virtual flag back from the folder cache
and becomes a saved search with the old scope and terms (bug 450059).

Fix: honor the folderIsDead flag when clearing the folder loading state.
close(folderIsDead) now passes it through to _setFolderLoading, which
skips startFolderLoading()/endFolderLoading() for dead folders. Our own
loading state and the listener are still updated, so the next view open
starts from a clean state and the UI's loading state stays in sync.

This only affects the dead-folder path; live folders keep the exact
previous behavior (endFolderLoading still runs from _folderLoaded and
from a normal mid-load close). Moving a folder to the trash is not
affected: that goes through folderMoveCopyCompleted -> _folderMoved,
which never calls close().

As part of this change, the folderLoading getter/setter is converted
into an isFolderLoading() method and a private _setFolderLoading()
method so that the "folder being deleted" flag can be passed without a
side-effectful setter.

A regression test (mail/base/test/unit/test_viewWrapper_virtualFolderDeleted.js)
opens a virtual folder in a DBViewWrapper, deletes it while it is
displayed and checks that the folder cache entry is not re-added and
that a folder created with the same name afterwards does not inherit the
Virtual flag. Without this fix the test fails: the deleted folder's
endFolderLoading re-adds its entry (with the Virtual flag) to the folder
cache.

To make sure a reused folder object behaves correctly after such an
abandoned load, nsMsgDBFolder::SetParent now resets the database-listener
state when a parentless folder is re-added to the tree. Without this, a
non-virtual folder deleted while it was loading would not re-attach its
database listener after being reused for a new folder with the same name.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315858


